# Reading CSV Files in Apache Flink

## Overview

This skill covers reading CSV data from files (including gzipped files) in Apache Flink, parsing them into POJOs, and setting up proper source functions for stream processing.

## SourceFunction for Gzipped CSV Files

### Basic SourceFunction Implementation

```java
import org.apache.flink.streaming.api.functions.source.SourceFunction;
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.io.InputStreamReader;
import java.util.zip.GZIPInputStream;

public class TaskEventSource implements SourceFunction<TaskEvent> {
    private final String filePath;
    private volatile boolean isRunning = true;

    public TaskEventSource(String filePath) {
        this.filePath = filePath;
    }

    @Override
    public void run(SourceContext<TaskEvent> ctx) throws Exception {
        BufferedReader reader;

        if (filePath.endsWith(".gz")) {
            reader = new BufferedReader(
                new InputStreamReader(
                    new GZIPInputStream(new FileInputStream(filePath))
                )
            );
        } else {
            reader = new BufferedReader(
                new InputStreamReader(new FileInputStream(filePath))
            );
        }

        String line;
        while (isRunning && (line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
            TaskEvent event = parseTaskEvent(line);
            if (event != null) {
                ctx.collect(event);
            }
        }
        reader.close();
    }

    @Override
    public void cancel() {
        isRunning = false;
    }

    private TaskEvent parseTaskEvent(String line) {
        String[] fields = line.split(",", -1);  // -1 to keep empty fields
        // Parse fields and create TaskEvent
        // Handle empty fields with proper null checks
        try {
            long timestamp = Long.parseLong(fields[0]);
            // ... parse other fields
            return new TaskEvent(timestamp, ...);
        } catch (NumberFormatException | ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException e) {
            return null;  // Skip malformed lines
        }
    }
}
```

## Parsing CSV with Empty Fields

### Handling Empty Fields in CSV

```java
private TaskEvent parseTaskEvent(String line) {
    String[] fields = line.split(",", -1);  // -1 keeps empty trailing fields

    // Parse required fields with defaults for empty values
    long timestamp = parseOrDefault(fields[0], 0L);
    String missingInfo = fields.length > 1 ? fields[1] : "";
    long jobId = parseOrDefault(fields[2], 0L);
    int taskIndex = parseIntOrDefault(fields[3], 0);

    // Optional machine ID (may be empty)
    Long machineId = fields.length > 4 && !fields[4].isEmpty()
        ? Long.parseLong(fields[4])
        : null;

    int eventType = parseIntOrDefault(fields[5], 0);

    return new TaskEvent(timestamp, missingInfo, jobId, taskIndex, machineId, eventType, ...);
}

private long parseOrDefault(String s, long defaultVal) {
    if (s == null || s.isEmpty()) return defaultVal;
    try {
        return Long.parseLong(s);
    } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
        return defaultVal;
    }
}

private int parseIntOrDefault(String s, int defaultVal) {
    if (s == null || s.isEmpty()) return defaultVal;
    try {
        return Integer.parseInt(s);
    } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
        return defaultVal;
    }
}

private double parseDoubleOrDefault(String s, double defaultVal) {
    if (s == null || s.isEmpty()) return defaultVal;
    try {
        return Double.parseDouble(s);
    } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
        return defaultVal;
    }
}
```

## Google Cluster Data Schema Reference

### Task Events Table (13 fields)

| Index | Field | Type |
|-------|-------|------|
| 0 | timestamp | long (microseconds) |
| 1 | missing info | string |
| 2 | job ID | long |
| 3 | task index | int |
| 4 | machine ID | long (optional) |
| 5 | event type | int |
| 6 | user name | string |
| 7 | scheduling class | int |
| 8 | priority | int |
| 9 | CPU request | double |
| 10 | memory request | double |
| 11 | disk space request | double |
| 12 | different-machine constraint | boolean (0/1) |

### Job Events Table (8 fields)

| Index | Field | Type |
|-------|-------|------|
| 0 | timestamp | long (microseconds) |
| 1 | missing info | string |
| 2 | job ID | long |
| 3 | event type | int |
| 4 | user name | string |
| 5 | scheduling class | int |
| 6 | job name | string |
| 7 | logical job name | string |

### Event Types

| Code | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| 0 | SUBMIT | Task/job became eligible for scheduling |
| 1 | SCHEDULE | Scheduled on a machine |
| 2 | EVICT | Descheduled due to higher priority |
| 3 | FAIL | Descheduled due to failure |
| 4 | FINISH | Completed normally |
| 5 | KILL | Cancelled by user/driver |
| 6 | LOST | Presumably terminated, record missing |
| 7 | UPDATE_PENDING | Updated while waiting to be scheduled |
| 8 | UPDATE_RUNNING | Updated while scheduled |

## Creating POJOs for Flink

### Requirements for Flink POJOs

1. Public class
2. Public no-arg constructor
3. All fields either public OR have public getters/setters
4. All field types must be serializable

### Example TaskEvent POJO

```java
public class TaskEvent implements Serializable {
    public long timestamp;
    public String missingInfo;
    public long jobId;
    public int taskIndex;
    public Long machineId;  // nullable
    public int eventType;
    public String userName;
    public int schedulingClass;
    public int priority;
    public double cpuRequest;
    public double memoryRequest;
    public double diskSpaceRequest;
    public int differentMachineConstraint;

    public TaskEvent() {} // Required for Flink

    public TaskEvent(long timestamp, String missingInfo, long jobId, int taskIndex,
                     Long machineId, int eventType, String userName, int schedulingClass,
                     int priority, double cpuRequest, double memoryRequest,
                     double diskSpaceRequest, int differentMachineConstraint) {
        this.timestamp = timestamp;
        this.missingInfo = missingInfo;
        this.jobId = jobId;
        this.taskIndex = taskIndex;
        this.machineId = machineId;
        this.eventType = eventType;
        this.userName = userName;
        this.schedulingClass = schedulingClass;
        this.priority = priority;
        this.cpuRequest = cpuRequest;
        this.memoryRequest = memoryRequest;
        this.diskSpaceRequest = diskSpaceRequest;
        this.differentMachineConstraint = differentMachineConstraint;
    }

    // Getters
    public long getTimestamp() { return timestamp; }
    public long getJobId() { return jobId; }
    public int getEventType() { return eventType; }
    // ... other getters as needed
}
```

## Using the Source in a Flink Job

```java
StreamExecutionEnvironment env = StreamExecutionEnvironment.getExecutionEnvironment();

DataStream<TaskEvent> taskEvents = env.addSource(new TaskEventSource(taskInputPath));

// Assign watermarks for event time processing
DataStream<TaskEvent> withWatermarks = taskEvents
    .assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(
        WatermarkStrategy
            .<TaskEvent>forBoundedOutOfOrderness(Duration.ofSeconds(10))
            .withTimestampAssigner((event, ts) -> event.getTimestamp() / 1000)  // Convert microseconds to milliseconds
    );
```

